cvcpkg: define a Jolt wheel's contact fields from construction.

JPH::Wheel leaves mContactPosition, mContactPointVelocity, mContactNormal,
mContactLongitudinal, mContactLateral and mAxlePlaneConstant uninitialized
(Jolt's Vec3 default constructor deliberately does not initialize) until the
wheel first touches the ground in VehicleConstraint::OnStep. But
VehicleConstraint::SaveState writes mContactPosition, mContactNormal and
mContactLateral for every wheel on every call. A vehicle saved before all its
wheels landed (every vehicle, for its first steps) therefore wrote heap
garbage into its saved state: two identical runs in one process saved, and
hashed, different bytes. Found by libcvc's physics replay test
(transfix/libcvc#698), where it broke the state hash for the first 8 steps.

The values match what libcvc's own workaround sets (defined_wheel), so a
consumer's state is the same with or without this patch: zero vectors, and a
zero axle-plane constant. mSuspensionLength is already initialized (to the
suspension's max length) by Wheel's constructor. Not yet reported upstream.

--- a/Jolt/Physics/Vehicle/Wheel.h
+++ b/Jolt/Physics/Vehicle/Wheel.h
@@ -125,12 +125,15 @@
 	SubShapeID				mContactSubShapeID;							///< Sub shape ID for ground
 	Body *					mContactBody = nullptr;						///< Body for ground
 	float					mSuspensionLength;							///< Current length of the suspension
-	RVec3					mContactPosition;							///< Position of the contact point between wheel and ground
-	Vec3					mContactPointVelocity;						///< Velocity of the contact point (m / s, not relative to the wheel but in world space)
-	Vec3					mContactNormal;								///< Normal of the contact point between wheel and ground
-	Vec3					mContactLongitudinal;						///< Vector perpendicular to normal in the forward direction
-	Vec3					mContactLateral;							///< Vector perpendicular to normal and longitudinal direction in the right direction
-	Real					mAxlePlaneConstant;							///< Constant for the contact plane of the axle, defined as ContactNormal . (WorldSpaceSuspensionPoint + SuspensionLength * WorldSpaceSuspensionDirection)
+	// cvcpkg: the contact fields below start defined. They are only written when the wheel
+	// touches the ground, but VehicleConstraint::SaveState writes three of them every step, so
+	// a vehicle whose wheels had not landed saved uninitialized memory into its state.
+	RVec3					mContactPosition = RVec3::sZero();		///< Position of the contact point between wheel and ground
+	Vec3					mContactPointVelocity = Vec3::sZero();		///< Velocity of the contact point (m / s, not relative to the wheel but in world space)
+	Vec3					mContactNormal = Vec3::sZero();				///< Normal of the contact point between wheel and ground
+	Vec3					mContactLongitudinal = Vec3::sZero();		///< Vector perpendicular to normal in the forward direction
+	Vec3					mContactLateral = Vec3::sZero();			///< Vector perpendicular to normal and longitudinal direction in the right direction
+	Real					mAxlePlaneConstant = 0;						///< Constant for the contact plane of the axle, defined as ContactNormal . (WorldSpaceSuspensionPoint + SuspensionLength * WorldSpaceSuspensionDirection)
 	float					mAntiRollBarImpulse = 0.0f;					///< Amount of impulse applied to the suspension from the anti-rollbars
 
 	float					mSteerAngle = 0.0f;							///< Rotation around the suspension direction, positive is to the left
